{"np_sdkfz250_10" "The SdKfz 250 was a light armoured halftrack built by the DEMAG firm, for use by Nazi Germany in World War II. The SdKfz 250/10 (37mm PaK) was the reconnaissance platoon leader's variant with 37mm PaK 35/36. This was the same anti-tank gun used in a towed carriage early in the war. It was normally used without the protective shield to conceal the firepower of this gun and look more like a SdKfz 250/1."}
; -- group d4 --
; [new] card "np_sdkfz250_9" cost 210 lvl 1 | soldiers vehicle_supporter x3 | tags 44 45 43 42 41 | units/ger/vehicles_44.set:92 | also under ger_ss/v3; cards np_sdkfz250_9, np_sdkfz250_9_ss
{"np_sdkfz250_9" "The SdKfz 250 was a light armoured halftrack very similar in appearance to the larger Hanomag-designed SdKfz 251 which was built by the DEMAG firm for use by Nazi Germany in World War II. SdKfz 250/9 - light armoured halftrack with 20mm KwK 30 gun."}
; -- group d6 --
; [new] card "np_sdkfz251_9" cost 280 lvl 1 | soldiers vehicle_supporter x3 | tags 44 45 43 42 41 | units/ger/vehicles_44.set:93 | also under ger_ss/v3; cards np_sdkfz251_9, np_sdkfz251_9_ss
{"np_sdkfz251_9"  "The SdKfz 251 (Sonderkraftfahrzeug 251) half-track was an armored fighting vehicle designed and first built by Nazi Germany's Hanomag company during World War II. They were produced throughout the war. This version was fitted with a 75 mm KwK 37 infantry support gun using the same pedestal gun mount employed on the StuG III. Nicknamed \"Stummel\" (\"stump\")."}
; -- group d15 --
; [new] card "np_sdkfz234_1" cost 265 lvl 1 | soldiers tankman x2, tankman2 | tags 44 45 | units/ger/vehicles_44.set:98 | also under ger_ss/v3; cards np_sdkfz234_1, np_sdkfz234_1_ss
{"np_sdkfz234_1" "The SdKfz 234 was an eight-wheeled armoured car used by the German Army in the Second World War. 234/1 - 1 x 20mm KwK 30 L/55 autocannon, 1 x MG 34 Machinegun. This design featured an open-topped turret. Around 200 were produced."}
; -- group d17 --
; [new] card "np_sdkfz234_3" cost 315 lvl 1 | soldiers tankman x2, tankman2 | tags 44 45 | units/ger/vehicles_44.set:99 | also under ger_ss/v3; cards np_sdkfz234_3, np_sdkfz234_3_ss
{"np_sdkfz234_3" "The SdKfz 234 was an eight-wheeled armoured car used by the German Army in the Second World War. 234/3 - 1 x 75mm K51 L/24 in open-topped superstructure replacing the turret. 88 built between June and December."}
; -- group d12 --
; [changed] card "pz2l" cost 220 lvl 1 | soldiers tankman x2, tankman2 | tags 44 45 43 | units/ger/vehicles_44.set:103 | also under ger_ss/v3, ger2/v3; cards pz2l, pz2l_ss, pz2l_ger2
{"pz2l" "The production of the Wehrmacht's last light tank began in 1942. The Lynx, with its 20mm autogun and light armor, did not pose a serious threat to enemy tanks, although its six-gear transmission allowed it to reach high speeds. Thanks to this advantage, it was ideally suited for reconnaissance missions which earned it deserved respect."}
; -- group d20 --
; [changed] card "ostwind" cost 300 lvl 1 | soldiers tankman x3, tankman2 | tags 44 45 | units/ger/vehicles_44.set:106
{"ostwind" "The PzKpfw IV's turret was removed and replaced with an open-top, hexagonal turret which housed a 37mm FlaK 43. In addition to its intended role as an anti-aircraft weapon, the fast-firing gun was highly effective against light vehicles and minor fortifications. A closed-top design would have been preferable, but this was not possible due to the heavy smoke generated by the gun."}
; -- group d5 --
; [new] card "np_sdkfz251_17" cost 220 lvl 1 | soldiers vehicle_supporter x3 | tags 45 43 42 41 | units/ger/vehicles_45.set:86 | also under ger_ss/v3; cards np_sdkfz251_17, np_sdkfz251_17_ss
{"np_sdkfz251_17" "The SdKfz 251 (Sonderkraftfahrzeug 251) half-track was an armored fighting vehicle designed and first built by Nazi Germany's Hanomag company during World War II. They were produced throughout the war. This version was fitted with a 20mm FlaK 38 anti-aircraft gun. Compared to the 20mm KwK 30, this gun has almost twice the cycling rate."}
